y check_response RAISES StructuredOutputError/UnretryableOutputError; S2 converts retryable ones to ModelRetry(message), so the original object is not necessarily chained onto the terminal UnexpectedModelBehavior","pydantic_ai.exceptions.UnexpectedModelBehavior resolves in the environment, but its cause-chain contents on output-retry exhaustion are not established by either ticket"],"finding":"The Approach premise that pydantic-ai's exhaustion exception carries the EXACT Rebar-owned StructuredOutputError/UnretryableOutputError object on its standard Python cause chain — the basis for the identity re-raise in AC2 — is an unverified pydantic-ai behavioral assertion. The S2 prerequisite [rebar:kingsize-unfair-blackbird] raises pydantic_ai.ModelRetry(message) from the output-fn/guard (which does not carry the original StructuredOutputError object) and describes exhaustion only as 'translated to a rebar-typed UnretryableOutputError' (a newly-constructed error), so neither S3 nor S2 establishes that the identical original object is present in the __cause__/__context__ chain to be found and re-raised.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f25273a1512fb3220","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('walk only the standard Python cause chain and re-raise the exact Rebar-owned StructuredOutputError object found there'); AC line 'Validation exhaustion re-raises the identical Rebar StructuredOutputError'","norm_id":"n94fb804cd6c40131","priority":0.75,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Validation exhaustion: the terminal UnexpectedModelBehavior's __cause__ is the last ModelRetry (or None), not the original Rebar StructuredOutputError, so the cause-chain walk finds no Rebar object to re-raise and AC2's identity guarantee cannot hold","Repeated output-size exhaustion where the terminal error was reconstructed rather than the original UnretryableOutputError object being chained"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify (and pin with a test) the exact chain hop by which the identical Rebar StructuredOutputError/UnretryableOutputError is reachable from the terminating UnexpectedModelBehavior — confirm the S2 adapter raises `ModelRetry(...) from <rebar error>` and that pydantic-ai chains UnexpectedModelBehavior to that ModelRetry — and define the fallback when the object is not on the chain.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'On exhaustion, walk only the standard Python cause chain and re-raise the exact Rebar-owned StructuredOutputError object found there, retaining the UnretryableOutputError subtype'","S2 ticket comment states UnexpectedModelBehavior is raised FRESH by consume_output_retry ('raises UnexpectedModelBehavior(\"Exceeded maximum output retries (N)\") when exceeded (lines 176-178)') — a fresh raise does not inherently place the last ModelRetry or the underlying Rebar error on __cause__","run_failure.py / failure.py walk __cause__ one level (failure.py:416,511), confirming the idiom but not the reachability of the specific Rebar object across the pydantic-ai ModelRetry boundary"],"finding":"The exhaustion-restoration mechanism assumes the exact Rebar StructuredOutputError/UnretryableOutputError object is reachable on the standard Python cause chain of the terminating UnexpectedModelBehavior, but the plan never establishes that pydantic-ai chains that fresh exception to the last ModelRetry, nor that the S2 adapter raised its ModelRetry with `from <rebar error>` so the object survives on __cause__. If either link is absent, the cause-chain walk finds nothing to re-raise and AC-2 (identity + subtype) fails.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1d6aea9bc3e59f47","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'walk only the standard Python cause chain and re-raise the exact Rebar-owned StructuredOutputError object found there'; AC-2","norm_id":"ne9520bebe282d701","priority":0.75,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Validation exhaustion where pydantic-ai's UnexpectedModelBehavior.__cause__ is the ModelRetry (message string) rather than the StructuredOutputError, or is None","Repeated output-size exhaustion where the concision ModelRetry did not chain the original UnretryableOutputError with `from`"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State how many __cause__ hops are walked and what each hop is (UnexpectedModelBehavior -> ModelRetry -> Rebar error), require the S2 output/guard seams to preserve the Rebar object via `raise ModelRetry(...) from err`, and define the behavior when no Rebar object is found (e.g. leave the UnexpectedModelBehavior untranslated) so the negative-guard test has a defined outcome.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"ye